<p>
  Shared state is a <code>Y.Array</code> of row <code>Y.Map</code>s, and every
  cell is its own <code>Y.Map</code> of <code>{ value, bold, fill }</code>. Edits
  to different cells merge, and edits to different properties of the same cell
  merge too — bold a cell while someone else is typing in it and both land. Set
  the same property twice and the last write wins. Values commit on Enter or
  blur, the way a spreadsheet does.
</p>
<p>
  Sorting and column order come from TanStack Table and are never written to the
  document: they are your view, not shared state. Sort by Owner in one window and
  by Qty in the other, then edit the same cell in both.
</p>
